[Verse 1 — human voice]
Back up the folders, one by one.
Name every file before it’s done.
A little drive beside the keys,
A pocket-sized machine at ease.
[Vocoder response]
Copy complete.
Check the space.
[Verse 2 — human voice]
The blue light waits beside the screen.
A quiet room, a steady green.
We choose the disk, we make the call,
A patient line across it all.
[Vocoder response]
Write the image.
Wait for change.
[Chorus — human voice]
We kept saying: any year.
Now the future’s running here.
[Vocoder response]
New system.
Same machine.
[Human voice]
All those years.
One small drive.
[Vocoder response]
Oh-mah-che.
Coming alive.
[Verse 3 — human voice]
The letters turn, then rearrange.
A loading bar begins to change.
The room stays still, the clock moves on,
Then one last prompt says: carry on.
[Vocoder response]
Install complete.
Open the door.
[Chorus — human voice]
We kept saying: any year.
Now the future’s running here.
[Vocoder response]
New system.
Same machine.
[Human voice]
All those years.
One small drive.
[Vocoder response]
Oh-mah-che.
Coming alive.
[Instrumental — sequencer-led]
[Outro — human voice]
A clean new window,
a softer start.
The little drive goes back in the drawer.
[Vocoder response]
Ready.
[Outro — human voice]
Ready for tomorrow.
